Dot Files
===

Shared config for my Fedora machines (legion, glass, teravangian) and my MacBook Air.

Set up a machine:

    git clone https://github.com/Jearil/dot.git ~/Projects/dot
    cd ~/Projects/dot
    ./install

Everyday commands:

    dot status               Show local changes and whether this machine is ahead or behind
    dot sync                 Pull and re-run the install
    dot packages             Install core packages (--flatpak adds the Flatpak list)
    dot kde                  Apply shared KDE settings
    dot macos                Apply macOS system preferences

Where things go:

    shell/, zsh/, bash/      Shared on every machine
    os/, tmux/               Linux and macOS differences
    hosts/<hostname>/        One machine only
    ~/.zshrc, ~/.bashrc      Machine-local lines and installer additions, never in the repo
    ~/.gitconfig.local       Machine-local git settings

~/.zshrc and ~/.bashrc are real files with one "dot-managed" line that sources the repo.
Installers can append to them without touching the repo.

btop and Zed rewrite their own configs, so config/ only seeds them on machines that don't
have them yet.

Secrets never go in this repo, which is public. They live in ~/.secrets (mode 700) and are
restored by hand from Bitwarden:

    glass, legion(if needed), teravangian   anthropic.env, teravangian-mobile.env,
                                            teravangian-mobile-keystore.env, twa-keystore.env
    teravangian                             coppermind.env

Don't put this repo in Syncthing, because it can corrupt .git.
